<template><heading>Outermost Code</heading><keywords><li>doctype</li><li>meta</li></keywords><section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>This unnamed fragment is the assembly root for the single-file application. It keeps the HTML document structure visible in one place while named references let the implementation be explained in a different order. Using one assembly root is an organizational choice, not a requirement of HTML or the tangler.</p>
        <p>Unit definitions run before the body is parsed; startup is deferred until the <a href="#23.lp5">templates</a> and <a href="#22.lp5">page elements</a> exist. Constructors therefore define services without trying to mount UI. The <a href="#25.lp5">startup article</a> explains initialization and failure reporting.</p>
    </section><section data-lp5-kind="code"><name/><code><![CDATA[<!doctype html>
<!-- lp5.html <>  -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" >
    <title>lp5</title>
    <style>
        ]]><lp5- ref="Global CSS declarations"/><![CDATA[
    </style>
    <script>
        "use strict";
        window.LP5 = (function () {
            ]]><lp5- ref="JavaScript units"/><![CDATA[
            return {
                ]]><lp5- ref="Outermost scope object names"/><![CDATA[
                };
        })();
    </script>
</head>
<body>
    ]]><lp5- ref="DOM declarations"/><![CDATA[
    ]]><lp5- ref="Dialog templates"/><![CDATA[
